WEBVTT

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.793
Its trajectory is erratic.

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:06.635
And our sensors aren't detecting
any stellar or planetary

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.971
gravitational fields that could
account for its motion.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:11.204
Then you're saying
it isn't a comet.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:15.408
And yet, it looks, feels and
tastes just like a comet.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.143
Well, there's a slight chance

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:20.118
there are magnetodynamic forces
acting on the comet

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.747
that are too subtle
for our sensors to detect.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.987
Or it might be something
we've never encountered before.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.890
B'Elanna, go down
to Transporter Room 2.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.192
Let's beam aboard a sample
for examination.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.664
Aye, Captain.

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:35.190
Harry, see if you
can lock onto a core fragment.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.964
Having no trouble penetrating
the crust, Captain.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:41.269
Janeway to Torres.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.241
We're ready when you are,
Lieutenant.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.767
Setting up a class-3
containment field, Captain.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.211
Field in place.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.805
Commence transport.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.042
Energizing.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.956
Hello.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.761
My name is Q.

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:58.443
Torres to Janeway.

00:02:58.477 --> 00:03:00.468
You'd better get down here,
Captain.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.707
Problem, Lieutenant?

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:02.714
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:04.716
That transport from the comet...

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:05.876
it brought a man aboard.

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:09.183
He says his name is Q.

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:11.689
Red Alert.
I'll be right down.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.417
Oh, please don't bother,
Captain.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.361
Let me take you
to lunch instead.

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:23.961
What a pleasure
it is to meet you.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.367
Oh, am I doing this right?

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:28.737
It's been so long since I've had
the opportunity to greet anyone.

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:31.572
Oh, uh... here.
Take a seat.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.669
Allow me to make the
setting more appropriate.

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:37.841
My name is Kathryn Janeway

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:38.872
Captain of the Federation...

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.613
Federation Starship Voyager.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.280
Yes, yes.
I know all that.

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:44.721
Look... Welsh rabbit

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.622
like your grandfather
used to make.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:50.095
Rabbit? She never told me
she likes rabbits.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:52.427
What is a rabbit, anyway?

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:53.989
Is this some new chef
she's interviewing?

00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:55.328
Please, eat.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:57.358
It's the least I can do
to express my appreciation.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.337
Appreciation for what?

00:03:59.371 --> 00:04:01.396
For letting me out
of my captivity.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.240
You were being held
against your will

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:06.403
inside the comet?

00:04:06.445 --> 00:04:08.379
In a manner of speaking.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.814
And you...

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.148
all of you...

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:16.518
you're mortals, aren't you?

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.682
Who was holding you prisoner?

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.317
And you...

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:25.853
only live for nine years.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:26.956
That's right.

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:29.194
Oh, how I envy you.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:30.566
Why is that?

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:34.699
Because the one thing
I want more than any other

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.901
is to die.

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:40.378
Look... I don't know
what you want here,

00:04:40.412 --> 00:04:42.676
but I know who you are.

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:43.773
Every Captain in Starfleet

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.306
has been briefed
about your appearances

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.784
on the Enterprise,
and I'm warning...

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:49.481
My... my appearances?

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:53.219
Oh, you've mistaken me for...

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:56.228
Oh, well, no matter.

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.093
I really must get on
with my business

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.462
before the others
realize I'm here.

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:05.202
When someone
asks you about me,

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:08.536
and they will,
would you tell them I said...

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.098
You know, I've had 300 years

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:12.076
to think of appropriate
last words.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:14.807
I wanted something... memorable,

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:16.678
you know?
Quotable.

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:21.315
Would you tell them I said,

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:24.516
"I die not for myself

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.252
but for you."

00:05:29.061 --> 00:05:30.187
I know.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:31.821
I... I know.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:33.832
Enigmatic, provocative.

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:36.164
They'll understand.

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:39.069
Well... good-bye to you all.

00:05:39.104 --> 00:05:41.299
Many thanks.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:44.036
Here's the end of me.

00:05:48.113 --> 00:05:51.412
Oh... dear.
That's not right.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.815
Torres to Janeway.

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:54.341
All the men have disappeared.

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:55.478
I'm aware of it, Lieutenant.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:56.886
Report to the Bridge.
Janeway out.

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:58.583
Bring them back now.

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:01.092
Oh, oh. Of course, of course.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.858
I'm... a little out of practice.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.941
Well... that's that,
I'm afraid... they're gone.

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:18.703
Gone? Where?

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:21.542
Just... gone.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.070
Oh, I apologize

00:06:23.115 --> 00:06:24.548
for the inconvenience.

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:30.782
Well, good luck to you all.

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:32.290
I really have to be going now.

00:06:32.324 --> 00:06:34.656
Return my crew.

00:06:34.693 --> 00:06:36.320
I...

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:38.557
I'm not sure how.

00:06:38.597 --> 00:06:42.055
Humans...

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:44.569
humans...

00:06:44.603 --> 00:06:48.198
Who would have more recent
experience with humans?

00:06:50.909 --> 00:06:53.173
What have you done now, Q?

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:06.151
Well, now, isn't this just fine.

00:07:06.191 --> 00:07:07.852
Humans aren't supposed
to be in this Quadrant

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:09.224
for another hundred years.

00:07:09.261 --> 00:07:11.729
I didn't bring them here.
Nothing to do with me.

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.823
How did you get out, Q?

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:15.299
I'm afraid
we're responsible for that.

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.768
Oh, well, I guess that's what
we get for having a woman

00:07:17.803 --> 00:07:18.929
in the Captain's seat.

00:07:19.038 --> 00:07:20.300
You know, I was betting

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:22.432
that Riker would
get this command.

00:07:22.474 --> 00:07:25.773
May I assume you're the Q
I've heard so much about?

00:07:25.811 --> 00:07:28.075
Have you heard about little me?

00:07:28.113 --> 00:07:29.341
Oh, do tell.

00:07:29.381 --> 00:07:32.612
Has Jean-Luc been whispering
about me behind my back?

00:07:34.687 --> 00:07:37.417
Say, is this a ship
of the Valkyries

00:07:37.456 --> 00:07:38.821
or have you human women

00:07:38.857 --> 00:07:42.054
finally done away
with your men altogether?

00:07:42.094 --> 00:07:43.721
There was a slight accident.

00:07:43.762 --> 00:07:45.161
A slight accident?

00:07:45.197 --> 00:07:46.824
Oh, let me guess.

00:07:46.865 --> 00:07:48.594
You were trying
to commit suicide.

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:51.763
Now you see why
we've locked him up

00:07:51.804 --> 00:07:52.964
for the last 300 years.

00:08:00.979 --> 00:08:02.913
Facial art!

00:08:02.981 --> 00:08:05.449
Ooh, how very wilderness of you.

00:08:05.484 --> 00:08:07.145
Captain?

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:09.916
All right, Q,
we should be going.

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:11.250
I'm not leaving.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.918
Captain Janeway,
I demand asylum.

00:08:13.959 --> 00:08:15.449
This is a joke.

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:16.688
No, it isn't.

00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:19.061
I am officially asking you,
Captain, to grant me asylum

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:22.625
and give me protection
from my enemies, which is him.

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:26.035
You would ask these puny humans
to protect you from me?

00:08:26.071 --> 00:08:27.368
Fat chance.

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:30.067
What did you do to him?

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:31.633
Nothing.

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:33.611
He's still there
in the 24th century.

00:08:33.645 --> 00:08:36.876
I just took the rest of us
to an old hiding place of mine.

00:08:38.083 --> 00:08:39.573
Report.

00:08:39.618 --> 00:08:42.712
Captain, there are
no stars outside.

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:44.416
Well, that's partially accurate.

00:08:44.456 --> 00:08:46.390
Actually, there's no universe
outside.

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:48.689
On screen.

00:08:48.727 --> 00:08:50.285
Commander?

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:54.527
I'm showing a large buildup
of baryonic particles.

00:08:54.566 --> 00:08:56.966
Perfectly normal.

00:08:57.069 --> 00:08:58.468
Captain, based on our readings,

00:08:58.504 --> 00:09:00.597
it appears we've been
transported back in time

00:09:00.639 --> 00:09:02.038
to the birth of the universe.

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:07.101
Very old hiding place.

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:09.239
Oh, I know all
the hiding places, Q.

00:09:09.281 --> 00:09:13.411
I hid here from the Continuum
myself once.

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:16.250
This ship will not survive
the formation of the cosmos.

00:09:16.288 --> 00:09:18.654
Yes, but just think of the honor
of having your DNA spread

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:20.681
from one corner
of the universe to the other.

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:24.025
Why, you could be the origin
of the humanoid form.

00:09:24.062 --> 00:09:26.860
Q... either Q...
get us out of here.

00:09:26.899 --> 00:09:29.629
You heard the lady, Q...
back to your cell.

00:09:32.938 --> 00:09:34.303
We're under attack.

00:09:34.339 --> 00:09:35.465
By a ship?

00:09:35.507 --> 00:09:38.067
By... by...

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.941
I'm not sure what they are.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.413
Captain, I don't believe this,

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:47.545
but according to my readings,
we're being attacked by protons.

00:09:47.586 --> 00:09:49.816
We've been reduced
to subatomic proportions.

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:51.288
He'll never find us here.

00:09:52.691 --> 00:09:54.352
Mr. Tuvok,
see if you can release

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:56.793
a positive ion charge
to repel them.

00:09:57.796 --> 00:09:59.991
Ready or not, here I am.

00:10:01.066 --> 00:10:02.863
Now what?

00:10:02.901 --> 00:10:04.459
Checking.

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:08.337
We seem to be tethered
to some kind of large...

00:10:08.373 --> 00:10:09.704
plant.

00:10:11.009 --> 00:10:12.670
Let's see it.

00:10:16.748 --> 00:10:18.875
Computer, I need a wider angle.

00:10:30.295 --> 00:10:32.695
You can't hide from me, Q.

00:10:32.731 --> 00:10:34.631
And you can't take me by force.

00:10:34.666 --> 00:10:37.134
I'll stalemate you for eternity
if I have to.

00:10:37.169 --> 00:10:38.864
The hell you will.

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:40.997
The vaunted Q Continuum...

00:10:41.073 --> 00:10:43.769
self-anointed guardians
of the universe.

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:45.208
How dare you come
aboard this ship

00:10:45.244 --> 00:10:48.008
and endanger this crew
with your personal tug-of-war?

00:10:48.113 --> 00:10:51.173
Did anyone ever tell you you're
angry when you're beautiful?

00:10:53.352 --> 00:10:55.013
We're back where we
started from, Captain.

00:10:55.053 --> 00:10:56.020
Doesn't matter.

00:10:56.054 --> 00:10:57.453
I'm not going back
into that cell.

00:10:57.489 --> 00:10:59.013
How would you like
to spend eternity

00:10:59.091 --> 00:11:01.025
as a Gorokian midwife toad?

00:11:01.059 --> 00:11:03.687
Oh, just try it.

00:11:03.729 --> 00:11:05.959
Stop.

00:11:06.064 --> 00:11:07.895
You want asylum?

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:09.628
Fine.
We'll have a hearing.

00:11:09.668 --> 00:11:11.295
A hearing!

00:11:11.336 --> 00:11:15.170
You would have me put his future
into your delicate little hands?

00:11:15.207 --> 00:11:18.108
Oh, so touchably soft.

00:11:18.143 --> 00:11:19.872
What is your secret, dear?

00:11:19.912 --> 00:11:23.279
When the Captain
of a Starfleet vessel receives

00:11:23.315 --> 00:11:25.909
an official request for asylum,
there is a clear

00:11:25.951 --> 00:11:26.975
procedure to follow.

00:11:27.019 --> 00:11:30.716
I suggest, to end your deadlock
and to save my ship,

00:11:30.756 --> 00:11:33.224
that we follow it to the letter.

00:11:33.258 --> 00:11:36.489
Well, this could go on for
a millennium or two, I suppose.

00:11:36.528 --> 00:11:39.190
All right, I accept
on behalf of the Continuum

00:11:39.231 --> 00:11:40.994
on one condition...

00:11:41.033 --> 00:11:42.364
if you rule in our favor,

00:11:42.401 --> 00:11:45.097
Q agrees to return
to his confinement.

00:11:45.137 --> 00:11:46.695
I have a condition of my own.

00:11:46.738 --> 00:11:48.706
If you rule in my favor,

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:52.232
then the Continuum
must grant me mortality.

00:11:52.277 --> 00:11:53.744
Why?
So you can kill yourself?

00:11:53.779 --> 00:11:54.677
Exactly.

00:11:54.713 --> 00:11:55.645
Accepted.

00:11:57.316 --> 00:11:59.546
Well, this is going to make
for an amusing diversion.

00:11:59.585 --> 00:12:02.748
Will you send him to prison
for eternity

00:12:02.788 --> 00:12:06.224
or will you assist
in his suicide plan?

00:12:06.258 --> 00:12:07.953
That's a toughie,

00:12:07.993 --> 00:12:10.427
but then again, that's why
they made you Captain, isn't it?

00:12:10.462 --> 00:12:12.760
To handle the real tough ones.

00:12:12.798 --> 00:12:15.926
My, my. Now I guess
we get to find out

00:12:15.968 --> 00:12:18.300
whether the pants...

00:12:18.337 --> 00:12:20.168
really fit.

00:12:27.646 --> 00:12:29.807
Am I interrupting anything?

00:12:29.848 --> 00:12:31.372
I am curious.

00:12:31.416 --> 00:12:33.850
Have the Q always had
an absence of manners,

00:12:33.885 --> 00:12:34.909
or is it the result

00:12:34.953 --> 00:12:37.114
of some natural
evolutionary process

00:12:37.155 --> 00:12:39.089
that comes with omnipotence?

00:12:39.124 --> 00:12:40.523
What?

00:12:40.559 --> 00:12:44.188
Oh, you mean just popping in
whenever we feel like it?

00:12:44.229 --> 00:12:46.959
That is one relevant example.

00:12:46.999 --> 00:12:49.559
I apologize.
At some point along the way,

00:12:49.601 --> 00:12:52.866
I guess we just stopped thinking
about the little niceties.

00:12:52.904 --> 00:12:54.269
So it seems.

00:12:54.306 --> 00:12:56.706
But you mustn't
think of us as omnipotent,

00:12:56.742 --> 00:12:59.802
no matter what the Continuum
would like you to believe.

00:12:59.845 --> 00:13:01.779
You and your ship seem
incredibly powerful

00:13:01.813 --> 00:13:03.474
to life-forms without
your technical expertise.

00:13:03.515 --> 00:13:05.483
It's no different with us.

00:13:05.517 --> 00:13:10.321
We may appear omnipotent to you,
but believe me, we're not.

00:13:10.454 --> 00:13:11.443
Intriguing.

00:13:11.488 --> 00:13:14.389
Just what vulnerabilities
do the Q have?

00:13:15.826 --> 00:13:18.693
Always looking for the tactical
advantage, Mr. Tuvok.

00:13:18.729 --> 00:13:20.253
Very good.

00:13:20.297 --> 00:13:23.960
As a matter of fact,
that's why I've come to see you.

00:13:24.068 --> 00:13:28.402
In a way, our vulnerability
is what this is all about.

00:13:28.439 --> 00:13:29.463
As the Q have evolved,

00:13:29.506 --> 00:13:31.497
we've sacrificed many things
along the way...

00:13:31.542 --> 00:13:35.979
not just manners, but mortality
and a sense of purpose

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:39.641
and a desire for change
and a capacity to grow.

00:13:39.683 --> 00:13:43.779
Each loss is
a new vulnerability...

00:13:43.821 --> 00:13:45.755
wouldn't you say?

00:13:45.789 --> 00:13:47.450
Why are you telling me this?

00:13:47.491 --> 00:13:50.983
Because I want you
to represent me at the hearing.

00:13:51.028 --> 00:13:52.757
Me?

00:13:52.796 --> 00:13:54.923
I have no legal expertise.

00:13:54.965 --> 00:13:56.455
But I need someone
who understands

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.661
Federation asylum practices.

00:13:58.702 --> 00:14:00.397
Besides...

00:14:00.437 --> 00:14:02.530
Vulcans approve of suicide.

00:14:02.573 --> 00:14:05.041
It is true that Vulcans

00:14:05.075 --> 00:14:06.940
who reach a certain infirmity
with age

00:14:07.044 --> 00:14:08.944
do practice ritual suicides.

00:14:09.012 --> 00:14:10.946
Nevertheless, I fail to see

00:14:11.048 --> 00:14:12.242
how that fact
would be meaningful

00:14:12.282 --> 00:14:13.476
in this circumstance.

00:14:15.386 --> 00:14:18.082
I have the right to counsel,
Mr. Tuvok.

00:14:18.122 --> 00:14:19.919
Will you assist me?

00:14:30.134 --> 00:14:31.965
Let me begin by stating clearly

00:14:32.002 --> 00:14:34.402
that I expect all parties
to act appropriately

00:14:34.438 --> 00:14:36.702
and with respect
for these proceedings.

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:39.106
I will not have this hearing
turned into a circus.

00:14:39.143 --> 00:14:40.337
Is that clear?

00:14:45.249 --> 00:14:46.409
Is that clear, Q?

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:50.352
Madam Captain,
we are dealing here

00:14:50.387 --> 00:14:53.083
with an issue of the greatest
importance to the Q Continuum.

00:14:53.123 --> 00:14:56.251
I can assure you, we take
this matter very seriously.

00:14:56.293 --> 00:14:57.260
Thank you.

00:14:57.294 --> 00:14:59.125
And please don't call me
"Madam Captain."

00:15:02.599 --> 00:15:04.123
Since you've made it clear

00:15:04.168 --> 00:15:06.398
that your asylum
would lead to suicide,

00:15:06.437 --> 00:15:08.598
you place me
in a difficult position.

00:15:08.639 --> 00:15:10.834
I understand, Captain.

00:15:10.874 --> 00:15:13.365
May I ask you
why you want to commit suicide?

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:16.072
As difficult as it is
for you to imagine,

00:15:16.113 --> 00:15:18.047
for me, immortality
is impossible

00:15:18.081 --> 00:15:19.708
to endure any longer.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:20.944
In the Continuum,

00:15:21.051 --> 00:15:22.575
an individual has an obligation

00:15:22.619 --> 00:15:25.782
to be responsible to the path
his life will follow.

00:15:25.823 --> 00:15:27.051
"His life will follow."

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:28.648
Emphasize life.

00:15:28.692 --> 00:15:32.458
I never yielded that obligation
to the Continuum.

00:15:32.496 --> 00:15:34.623
If the path I choose
leads to death,

00:15:34.665 --> 00:15:36.599
what right have they
to interfere?

00:15:36.633 --> 00:15:38.191
He's putting his selfish wishes

00:15:38.235 --> 00:15:39.964
above the welfare
of everyone else.

00:15:40.003 --> 00:15:41.300
And if I don't agree
with the majority,

00:15:41.338 --> 00:15:43.966
I'm to be locked up
for eternity.

00:15:44.074 --> 00:15:45.063
You would not be confined

00:15:45.108 --> 00:15:47.975
if you were not intent
on harming yourself.

00:15:48.011 --> 00:15:49.603
With your permission, Captain,

00:15:49.646 --> 00:15:52.979
I would like to call
an expert on the Continuum

00:15:53.016 --> 00:15:56.543
to discuss the implications
of the decision to be made.

00:15:56.587 --> 00:15:57.611
Proceed.

00:15:57.654 --> 00:16:00.885
I call myself to the stand.

00:16:02.159 --> 00:16:03.456
Ta-da!

00:16:03.494 --> 00:16:04.620
Thank you for coming.

00:16:04.661 --> 00:16:06.595
It's a rare honor

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:09.497
to have someone of your
reputation and accomplishment

00:16:09.533 --> 00:16:10.500
with us today.

00:16:10.534 --> 00:16:11.933
Thank you.

00:16:12.035 --> 00:16:16.199
Tell me, what would be the
impact of a Q suicide?

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.470
Oh, it would be an interruption
to the Continuum.

00:16:18.509 --> 00:16:20.943
It would change the very nature
of Q.

00:16:20.978 --> 00:16:22.809
Can you be more specific?

00:16:22.846 --> 00:16:26.373
No, because we're not even sure
what the end result would be.

00:16:26.416 --> 00:16:29.442
His suicide could have all sorts
of unknown consequences

00:16:29.486 --> 00:16:30.578
for the Continuum.

00:16:30.621 --> 00:16:32.213
Precisely!

00:16:32.256 --> 00:16:35.157
It would force the Q
to deal with the unknown

00:16:35.192 --> 00:16:37.660
for the first time
since the new era began.

00:16:37.694 --> 00:16:38.888
They're afraid of me

00:16:38.929 --> 00:16:42.524
because they're afraid
of the unknown.

00:16:42.566 --> 00:16:44.727
How would you characterize
his remarks?

00:16:44.768 --> 00:16:48.499
No Q has ever tried
to commit suicide.

00:16:48.539 --> 00:16:52.669
Immortality is one of the
defining qualities of being a Q.

00:16:52.709 --> 00:16:55.075
By every measure
of the Continuum,

00:16:55.112 --> 00:16:57.774
his remarks would have
to be considered as...

00:16:57.814 --> 00:16:59.975
mentally unbalanced.

00:17:00.017 --> 00:17:02.349
Mentally unbalanced.

00:17:02.386 --> 00:17:04.820
And no civilized people
in the universe,

00:17:04.855 --> 00:17:07.346
including the primitive
Federation societies,

00:17:07.391 --> 00:17:12.351
would condone the suicide
of a mentally unbalanced person.

00:17:12.396 --> 00:17:15.297
Tell me, Q,

00:17:15.332 --> 00:17:17.892
can you offer any other evidence
of mental instability

00:17:17.935 --> 00:17:19.630
on the part of my client?

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:21.103
What more do I need?

00:17:21.138 --> 00:17:22.901
He wants to kill himself.

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:25.909
In fact, until this issue arose,
he was known in the Continuum

00:17:25.943 --> 00:17:27.570
as one of your great
philosophers.

00:17:27.611 --> 00:17:29.408
- Is that not true?
- Not anymore it isn't.

00:17:29.446 --> 00:17:32.904
So your entire basis for
judging him mentally unbalanced

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:35.043
is his wish to commit suicide.

00:17:35.085 --> 00:17:37.679
I submit
that is a faulty premise.

00:17:37.721 --> 00:17:40.189
In many cultures,
suicide is acceptable

00:17:40.223 --> 00:17:42.783
and in and of itself
cannot be used as evidence

00:17:42.826 --> 00:17:45.317
of mental illness.

00:17:45.362 --> 00:17:48.388
I tend to agree with Mr. Tuvok.

00:17:48.432 --> 00:17:50.957
- Oh... Vulcans!
- Oh... Vulcans!

00:17:51.001 --> 00:17:53.094
Isn't it true that on occasion,

00:17:53.136 --> 00:17:55.866
the Continuum has executed Qs
for certain crimes?

00:17:55.906 --> 00:17:57.373
On rare occasions, yes.

00:17:57.407 --> 00:18:00.501
Didn't their deaths create an
interruption in the Continuum?

00:18:00.544 --> 00:18:01.772
Their crimes created
the interruption,

00:18:01.812 --> 00:18:02.779
their deaths ended it.

00:18:02.813 --> 00:18:04.371
I know where you're going
with this, Lieutenant.

00:18:04.414 --> 00:18:05.676
Do you?

00:18:05.716 --> 00:18:07.206
And it's not going to work.

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:08.478
Our society, like any other,

00:18:08.518 --> 00:18:10.645
must control
its disruptive elements.

00:18:10.687 --> 00:18:13.155
An execution may be undesirable,
I grant you that,

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:15.124
but on some rare occasions,

00:18:15.158 --> 00:18:17.820
it is necessary
and warranted, and a decision

00:18:17.861 --> 00:18:20.329
to proceed is made
only after great deliberation

00:18:20.364 --> 00:18:22.127
by the entire Continuum.

00:18:22.165 --> 00:18:25.362
You cannot imagine the chaos
that would be created

00:18:25.402 --> 00:18:27.370
if individuals like Q here

00:18:27.404 --> 00:18:29.395
could choose between
life and death.

00:18:29.439 --> 00:18:32.465
This is a matter of social order
versus anarchy.

00:18:32.509 --> 00:18:35.501
I understand.

00:18:35.545 --> 00:18:38.139
And you find
nothing contradictory

00:18:38.181 --> 00:18:40.672
in a society
that outlaws suicide

00:18:40.717 --> 00:18:43.208
but practices
capital punishment?

00:18:45.389 --> 00:18:46.879
No.

00:18:46.923 --> 00:18:48.823
Any other questions, Lieutenant?

00:18:55.832 --> 00:18:57.493
Just one other thing.

00:18:57.534 --> 00:18:58.967
Isn't it true that you yourself

00:18:59.069 --> 00:19:01.128
were once accused
of being mentally unstable

00:19:01.171 --> 00:19:02.138
by the Continuum?

00:19:02.172 --> 00:19:04.606
Were you not disciplined
for inappropriate behavior?

00:19:04.641 --> 00:19:05.630
Objection.

00:19:05.676 --> 00:19:07.576
I'll allow the question.

00:19:08.845 --> 00:19:11.211
My record has been expunged.

00:19:11.248 --> 00:19:13.045
I will take that as a yes.

00:19:13.083 --> 00:19:14.209
Thank you.

00:19:14.251 --> 00:19:15.843
That is all.

00:19:15.886 --> 00:19:17.410
You're excused.

00:19:18.622 --> 00:19:21.090
If I may beg
the court's indulgence,

00:19:21.124 --> 00:19:22.614
I have other witnesses to call.

00:19:22.659 --> 00:19:24.149
To what end?

00:19:24.194 --> 00:19:25.422
Your Captain Honor,

00:19:25.462 --> 00:19:27.930
I am here to argue
for the majesty of life...

00:19:27.998 --> 00:19:29.761
what it means
for us to be alive.

00:19:29.800 --> 00:19:32.792
A Q's life takes him
to all corners of the universe.

00:19:32.836 --> 00:19:36.897
This Q's life has touched and
affected many, many others...

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:39.101
including some
on your own homeworld.

00:19:39.142 --> 00:19:40.131
With your permission,

00:19:40.177 --> 00:19:42.077
I would like to call
some of those people

00:19:42.112 --> 00:19:45.047
whose lives have been
changed by this Q.

00:19:45.082 --> 00:19:47.744
You want to bring people here
from Earth?

00:19:47.784 --> 00:19:49.308
I promise
it won't impact the timeline,

00:19:49.352 --> 00:19:50.341
and no one will remember

00:19:50.387 --> 00:19:53.515
ever having been here
after I send them back.

00:19:53.557 --> 00:19:56.219
This is most unusual.

00:19:56.259 --> 00:19:58.284
Do you have any objection,
Mr. Tuvok?

00:19:58.328 --> 00:20:01.126
I am as curious
as you are, Captain.

00:20:03.734 --> 00:20:05.258
Very well.

00:20:05.435 --> 00:20:07.528
Proceed.

00:20:09.873 --> 00:20:11.864
Q!

00:20:11.908 --> 00:20:13.205
What the hell is going on?

00:20:13.243 --> 00:20:15.234
My apologies, Commander...

00:20:15.278 --> 00:20:16.768
To you all.

00:20:16.813 --> 00:20:19.543
My name is Kathryn Janeway.

00:20:19.583 --> 00:20:23.110
Captain Janeway,
the USS Voyager.

00:20:23.153 --> 00:20:25.587
That's correct, Commander.

00:20:25.622 --> 00:20:27.146
You're aboard Voyager.

00:20:27.190 --> 00:20:28.157
We're lost

00:20:28.191 --> 00:20:29.988
in the Delta Quadrant,
and as much as I wish

00:20:30.026 --> 00:20:31.789
you could tell them
that when you get home,

00:20:31.828 --> 00:20:34.956
your memories will be wiped
before you get back.

00:20:34.998 --> 00:20:36.989
God, if you let me
live through this,

00:20:37.067 --> 00:20:39.661
I promise I'll clean
up my act... I swear.

00:20:39.703 --> 00:20:41.330
I demand an explanation!

00:20:41.371 --> 00:20:43.669
Why are you dressed
like this, young man?

00:20:43.707 --> 00:20:45.834
Man, have you looked
in a mirror lately?

00:20:45.876 --> 00:20:47.810
Allow me to try to explain,
Mister?

00:20:47.844 --> 00:20:48.868
Ginsberg.

00:20:48.912 --> 00:20:51.813
Maury Ginsberg.

00:20:51.848 --> 00:20:54.214
Sir Isaac Newton.

00:20:54.251 --> 00:20:55.275
William Riker.

00:20:55.318 --> 00:20:56.285
Nice to meet you.

00:20:56.319 --> 00:20:59.914
Consider for a moment
that it might be possible

00:20:59.956 --> 00:21:04.120
to travel forward in time...
say, to the 24th century...

00:21:04.161 --> 00:21:05.890
onto a starship...

00:21:05.929 --> 00:21:10.229
75,000 light-years from Earth.

00:21:15.605 --> 00:21:17.971
You're having
a very strange dream

00:21:18.074 --> 00:21:20.372
and in this dream,
you are seeing this man

00:21:20.410 --> 00:21:22.071
whom you've all met before.

00:21:23.079 --> 00:21:24.979
Yes, I have seen
that man before.

00:21:25.048 --> 00:21:26.982
You were sitting
under the tree the day...

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:29.450
The day the apple
fell on your head.

00:21:29.486 --> 00:21:30.953
Yes, that's right.

00:21:30.987 --> 00:21:31.976
Quite a day, wasn't it?

00:21:32.055 --> 00:21:33.181
As a matter of fact,

00:21:33.223 --> 00:21:36.158
this man jostled the tree
when he got up to leave.

00:21:36.193 --> 00:21:38.627
Just before
the apple fell... yes.

00:21:38.662 --> 00:21:41.927
And a new era in human
science was born.

00:21:41.965 --> 00:21:44.866
Wait a minute!
Weren't you the guy in the jeep?

00:21:46.236 --> 00:21:49.103
The "guy in the jeep"

00:21:49.139 --> 00:21:51.471
who picked you up after
your own vehicle broke down

00:21:51.508 --> 00:21:52.532
that summer afternoon.

00:21:52.576 --> 00:21:53.543
Isn't that right?

00:21:53.577 --> 00:21:56.375
Oh, man, he was a lifesaver.

00:21:56.413 --> 00:21:58.108
My van died,
and they dragged it off the road

00:21:58.148 --> 00:21:59.206
because of all the traffic.

00:21:59.249 --> 00:22:00.307
It was backed up for miles.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:02.944
You were on your way to a job,
weren't you?

00:22:03.019 --> 00:22:05.681
Yeah, I was supposed to be on
the follow spot up in Tower 3.

00:22:05.722 --> 00:22:07.212
I never
would have made it in time

00:22:07.257 --> 00:22:08.224
if it weren't for him.

00:22:08.258 --> 00:22:10.488
Hey, whatever happened
with that groovy chick

00:22:10.527 --> 00:22:12.586
with the long red beads
in the back seat?

00:22:12.629 --> 00:22:15.154
I've been looking for her
ever since you dropped me off.

00:22:15.198 --> 00:22:18.292
You'll see her again,
don't worry.

00:22:18.335 --> 00:22:19.302
To sum up, you were

00:22:19.336 --> 00:22:22.237
a spotlight operator at an
outdoor concert of some sort,

00:22:22.272 --> 00:22:23.796
a concert
that was put in jeopardy

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:25.239
moments before it was to begin

00:22:25.275 --> 00:22:27.573
because the entire
sound system failed.

00:22:27.611 --> 00:22:28.737
Oh, it was no big deal.

00:22:28.778 --> 00:22:30.746
Somebody must have snagged
an extension cord

00:22:30.780 --> 00:22:32.748
with one of the trucks,
that's all.

00:22:32.782 --> 00:22:35.182
I'm just lucky I noticed it.

00:22:35.218 --> 00:22:38.278
Yes. Lucky you were at the right
place at the right time,

00:22:38.321 --> 00:22:40.152
or it would have taken days
to track down the problem

00:22:40.190 --> 00:22:41.452
and there would
have been no concert.

00:22:41.491 --> 00:22:43.982
Well, I'm sorry to say

00:22:44.060 --> 00:22:46.494
I have met him,
but I've never seen

00:22:46.529 --> 00:22:47.826
this man before in my life.

00:22:47.864 --> 00:22:48.956
Are you sure?

00:22:48.999 --> 00:22:50.489
Has it not been established

00:22:50.533 --> 00:22:53.195
that my client has been
in captivity during all

00:22:53.236 --> 00:22:54.464
of Commander Riker's lifetime?

00:22:54.504 --> 00:22:56.768
Have you seen
this photograph before?

00:22:59.943 --> 00:23:01.638
Sure I have.

00:23:01.678 --> 00:23:03.873
That is Colonel Thaddeus Riker

00:23:03.914 --> 00:23:05.939
after he was wounded
at Pine Mountain.

00:23:06.016 --> 00:23:08.177
They used to call him
"Old Iron Boots."

00:23:08.218 --> 00:23:10.550
He was in command
of the 102nd New York

00:23:10.587 --> 00:23:13.283
during General Sherman's
march on Atlanta.

00:23:13.323 --> 00:23:18.056
This picture was taken in 1864,
just after they let him out

00:23:18.094 --> 00:23:19.061
of the army hospital.

00:23:19.095 --> 00:23:20.497
And the soldier beside him?

00:23:24.634 --> 00:23:26.124
I'll be damned.

00:23:27.504 --> 00:23:28.471
It's him.

00:23:28.505 --> 00:23:30.939
As a matter of fact,

00:23:30.974 --> 00:23:35.411
he carried your wounded ancestor
back from the front line...

00:23:35.445 --> 00:23:36.639
Didn't you?

00:23:41.351 --> 00:23:42.477
My point is, Captain,

00:23:42.519 --> 00:23:45.545
Q has had a profound influence
on these three lives.

00:23:45.588 --> 00:23:46.987
Without Q,

00:23:47.090 --> 00:23:49.251
Isaac Newton would
have died forgotten

00:23:49.292 --> 00:23:51.192
in a Liverpool debtor's prison...

00:23:51.227 --> 00:23:54.628
a suspect in several
prostitute murders.

00:23:54.664 --> 00:23:56.598
Without Q,

00:23:56.633 --> 00:23:59.261
there would have been
no concert at, uh...

00:23:59.302 --> 00:24:00.792
Woodstock.

00:24:00.837 --> 00:24:02.270
Wherever.

00:24:02.305 --> 00:24:03.567
More importantly,

00:24:03.606 --> 00:24:05.938
Mr. Ginsberg would never
have met his future wife

00:24:05.975 --> 00:24:08.808
"the groovy chick
with the long red beads"

00:24:08.845 --> 00:24:11.177
and he would never have become
a successful orthodontist,

00:24:11.214 --> 00:24:13.307
settled in Scarsdale
with four kids.

00:24:13.349 --> 00:24:14.941
Far out.

00:24:14.984 --> 00:24:16.611
Yes.

00:24:16.653 --> 00:24:19.952
Without Q, there would have been
no William T. Riker at all,

00:24:20.056 --> 00:24:20.954
and I would have lost

00:24:21.057 --> 00:24:22.957
at least a dozen
really good opportunities

00:24:22.992 --> 00:24:25.324
to insult him over the years.

00:24:25.361 --> 00:24:27.693
Oh, and lest I forget...

00:24:27.730 --> 00:24:31.564
without Q, the Borg would
have assimilated the Federation.

00:24:31.601 --> 00:24:34.866
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:24:36.573 --> 00:24:39.406
This is the life that Q
treats without respect.

00:24:39.442 --> 00:24:42.104
This is the life that he would
give up so easily.

00:24:42.145 --> 00:24:44.943
May I remind this hearing
and my learned colleague,

00:24:44.981 --> 00:24:46.778
that for the last
three centuries,

00:24:46.816 --> 00:24:49.979
my client has not been
allowed contact with anyone.

00:24:50.086 --> 00:24:52.452
At this time, we would
like to reproduce

00:24:52.488 --> 00:24:54.388
the environment in which
he has been confined.

00:24:54.424 --> 00:24:55.322
I object.

00:24:55.358 --> 00:24:57.383
No...

00:24:57.427 --> 00:24:59.327
I'll allow this.

00:25:07.003 --> 00:25:08.493
These are the conditions

00:25:08.538 --> 00:25:10.938
my client will be forced
to live in for eternity

00:25:10.974 --> 00:25:12.566
if you deny him asylum, Captain.

00:25:12.609 --> 00:25:15.510
We just want to give him time
to reconsider his position.

00:25:15.545 --> 00:25:17.706
I will never change my mind!

00:25:17.747 --> 00:25:18.714
This is your own doing.

00:25:18.748 --> 00:25:20.340
You could live
a perfectly normal life

00:25:20.383 --> 00:25:22.681
if you were simply willing
to live a perfectly normal life.

00:25:22.719 --> 00:25:23.708
I've seen enough.

00:25:23.753 --> 00:25:26.017
Please return us
to the hearing room.

00:25:28.124 --> 00:25:30.388
I would submit
that the quality of life

00:25:30.426 --> 00:25:32.189
my client will have to endure

00:25:32.228 --> 00:25:33.889
should be considered
in this proceeding.

00:25:33.930 --> 00:25:37.866
I don't like those conditions
any more than you do, Mr. Tuvok,

00:25:37.900 --> 00:25:40.698
and I wouldn't want
to spend another day there

00:25:40.737 --> 00:25:41.795
if I were you, Q...

00:25:41.838 --> 00:25:46.468
but I'm here to rule
on a request for asylum,

00:25:46.509 --> 00:25:49.967
not to judge the penal system
of the Q Continuum.

00:25:50.046 --> 00:25:52.344
And he does have a point...

00:25:52.382 --> 00:25:56.546
you were confined to prevent you
from doing harm to yourself.

00:25:56.586 --> 00:25:59.885
I've been doing
a great deal of research,

00:25:59.922 --> 00:26:02.720
studying a variety
of cultural attitudes on suicide

00:26:02.759 --> 00:26:05.125
to help me frame the basis
of a decision.

00:26:05.161 --> 00:26:06.651
Mr. Tuvok, are you familiar

00:26:06.696 --> 00:26:09.096
with the "double effect"
principle on assisted suicide

00:26:09.132 --> 00:26:11.032
that dates back
to the Bolian middle ages?

00:26:11.067 --> 00:26:13.399
I believe it relates
to the relief of suffering,

00:26:13.436 --> 00:26:14.460
does it not, Captain?

00:26:14.504 --> 00:26:18.804
It states, "an action
that has the principle effect

00:26:18.841 --> 00:26:21.776
"of relieving suffering
may be ethically justified

00:26:21.811 --> 00:26:24.678
"even though the same action
has the secondary effect

00:26:24.714 --> 00:26:27.046
of possibly causing death."

00:26:27.083 --> 00:26:29.950
This principle is the only thing
I can find

00:26:30.019 --> 00:26:33.955
that could possibly convince me
to decide in your favor, Q.

00:26:33.990 --> 00:26:35.651
And yet, as I look at you,

00:26:35.692 --> 00:26:37.523
you don't seem,
by our standards,

00:26:37.560 --> 00:26:41.121
aged, infirm or in any pain.

00:26:41.164 --> 00:26:43.758
Can you show this hearing
that you suffer

00:26:43.800 --> 00:26:45.529
in any manner
other than that caused

00:26:45.568 --> 00:26:47.934
by the conditions
of your incarceration?

00:26:47.970 --> 00:26:52.566
Any suffering that would justify
a decision to grant you asylum?

00:26:57.413 --> 00:26:59.210
May I request a recess

00:26:59.248 --> 00:27:01.580
to consider our response,
Captain?

00:27:04.187 --> 00:27:05.779
Granted.

00:27:05.855 --> 00:27:07.823
We're going to lose, aren't we?

00:27:07.857 --> 00:27:11.793
I would say we have not yet
convinced Captain Janeway

00:27:11.828 --> 00:27:14.058
of the validity
of our argument.

00:27:14.097 --> 00:27:16.861
You're doing a fine job,
Mr. Tuvok.

00:27:16.899 --> 00:27:19.629
It's nice to know
someone believes in me.

00:27:19.669 --> 00:27:22.832
I am representing your position
to the best of my ability.

00:27:22.872 --> 00:27:26.035
It is most definitely
not my own.

00:27:26.075 --> 00:27:28.566
I see no persuasive evidence

00:27:28.611 --> 00:27:30.408
that a life like yours
should be wasted

00:27:30.446 --> 00:27:32.641
simply because
you are disgruntled.

00:27:32.682 --> 00:27:35.742
Frankly, I see no logic
to your position.

00:27:35.785 --> 00:27:37.753
You...

00:27:37.787 --> 00:27:40.221
you surprise me, Mr. Tuvok,

00:27:40.256 --> 00:27:43.953
which is a rare and special gift
to a Q. Thank you.

00:27:44.060 --> 00:27:49.293
But may I say, if only you knew
what life as a Q were like,

00:27:49.332 --> 00:27:50.959
you would see the logic.

00:27:51.067 --> 00:27:55.299
Then perhaps what we should do
next is take this hearing

00:27:55.338 --> 00:27:57.898
to see life
in the Continuum itself.

00:28:04.947 --> 00:28:06.608
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:28:06.649 --> 00:28:08.480
I'm determined
to find a better alternative

00:28:08.518 --> 00:28:10.577
to suicide or endless prison,

00:28:10.620 --> 00:28:14.078
so I've summoned the advocate Q
to make him a proposal.

00:28:14.123 --> 00:28:15.420
Yes, what is it, Captain?

00:28:15.458 --> 00:28:16.925
Come to the next session
of the hearing

00:28:16.993 --> 00:28:19.052
and announce
that the Continuum is ready

00:28:19.095 --> 00:28:21.529
to reintegrate Q
into your society...

00:28:21.564 --> 00:28:24.931
that you won't condemn him
to that cell for eternity.

00:28:25.001 --> 00:28:27.299
And you will rule in our favor?

00:28:27.336 --> 00:28:29.930
I would consider it
a very meaningful gesture

00:28:30.006 --> 00:28:31.439
by the Continuum.

00:28:31.474 --> 00:28:34.705
How would you know
if I intended to keep my word?

00:28:34.744 --> 00:28:38.942
Based on my research,
you have been many things...

00:28:38.981 --> 00:28:42.382
a rude, interfering,
inconsiderate, sadistic...

00:28:42.418 --> 00:28:43.385
You've made your point.

00:28:43.419 --> 00:28:44.784
...pest!

00:28:44.821 --> 00:28:45.913
And, oh, yes...

00:28:45.955 --> 00:28:49.413
you introduced us to the Borg...
thank you very much...

00:28:49.458 --> 00:28:52.950
but one thing you have
never been is a liar.

00:28:52.995 --> 00:28:57.830
I think you've uncovered
my one redeeming virtue.

00:28:57.867 --> 00:29:00.097
Am I blushing?

00:29:00.136 --> 00:29:03.765
I wish I could help you,
Kathy, I just can't.

00:29:03.806 --> 00:29:05.740
We're dealing here
with the most dangerous man

00:29:05.775 --> 00:29:06.764
in the Continuum.

00:29:06.809 --> 00:29:08.606
Now, I didn't tell you this,

00:29:08.644 --> 00:29:12.307
but one of his
self-destructive stunts

00:29:12.348 --> 00:29:13.406
created a misunderstanding

00:29:13.449 --> 00:29:15.747
which ignited the 100-year war

00:29:15.785 --> 00:29:18.219
between the Romulans
and the Vulcans.

00:29:18.254 --> 00:29:22.623
No. This man goes back
into his confinement,

00:29:22.658 --> 00:29:27.493
but... I would like to make it
easier for you.

00:29:27.530 --> 00:29:32.058
The Continuum is prepared
to do you a little favor...

00:29:33.569 --> 00:29:36.197
if we approve of your ruling.

00:29:37.807 --> 00:29:39.138
Look out the window.

00:29:52.555 --> 00:29:56.047
Now you see it, now you don't.

00:30:07.670 --> 00:30:09.661
We are prepared
to illustrate the nature

00:30:09.705 --> 00:30:11.104
of Q's suffering, Captain,

00:30:11.140 --> 00:30:13.665
but in order to do so,
we must show this hearing

00:30:13.709 --> 00:30:15.574
what life is like
in the Continuum.

00:30:15.611 --> 00:30:17.101
And how do you
intend to do that?

00:30:17.146 --> 00:30:20.377
By going to the Continuum
itself.

00:30:20.416 --> 00:30:22.281
Is this possible?

00:30:22.318 --> 00:30:23.410
No, it's a ridiculous idea.

00:30:23.452 --> 00:30:24.578
You would never understand.

00:30:24.620 --> 00:30:25.985
My client has the right to ask

00:30:26.088 --> 00:30:27.612
for an inspection
of the living conditions

00:30:27.657 --> 00:30:29.454
that lead to his suffering,
Captain.

00:30:29.492 --> 00:30:30.891
I would agree with that.

00:30:33.629 --> 00:30:34.926
I suppose you have
some crazy idea

00:30:34.964 --> 00:30:35.988
how to pull this off?

00:30:36.032 --> 00:30:37.021
Yes.

00:30:39.635 --> 00:30:40.829
Only if...

00:30:40.870 --> 00:30:42.201
Fine, fine.

00:30:43.739 --> 00:30:46.640
We've agreed on a format
for this little sojourn,

00:30:46.676 --> 00:30:48.940
but I still believe
it's ill-advised.

00:30:48.978 --> 00:30:51.412
I'll be the judge of that.

00:30:53.149 --> 00:30:55.083
Whenever you're ready.

00:30:56.619 --> 00:30:57.608
No, no.

00:31:02.825 --> 00:31:06.352
This is the Q Continuum...
a road in a desert?

00:31:06.395 --> 00:31:07.623
I told you so.

00:31:07.663 --> 00:31:10.131
This is a manifestation
of the Continuum

00:31:10.166 --> 00:31:13.294
that we hope falls within
your level of comprehension.

00:31:13.336 --> 00:31:15.497
This way.

00:31:55.911 --> 00:31:57.003
Good afternoon.

00:32:01.417 --> 00:32:04.352
I apologize for their lack
of hospitality, Captain.

00:32:04.387 --> 00:32:05.945
We're not used to visitors here.

00:32:06.055 --> 00:32:08.785
In fact, you're the only ones
who've ever come.

00:32:08.824 --> 00:32:10.951
Then what is the purpose
of the road?

00:32:10.993 --> 00:32:12.290
The road...

00:32:12.328 --> 00:32:14.762
takes us to the rest
of the universe,

00:32:14.797 --> 00:32:16.560
then it leads back here...

00:32:16.599 --> 00:32:18.897
an endless circle.

00:32:18.934 --> 00:32:21.698
This was your existence
before your confinement?

00:32:21.737 --> 00:32:24.797
I traveled the road
many times...

00:32:24.840 --> 00:32:27.206
sat on the porch,
played the games...

00:32:27.243 --> 00:32:29.837
been the dog... everything.

00:32:29.879 --> 00:32:31.574
I was even the scarecrow
for a while.

00:32:31.614 --> 00:32:33.172
Why?

00:32:33.215 --> 00:32:35.706
Because I hadn't done it.

00:32:35.751 --> 00:32:38.311
Oh, we've all done
the scarecrow. Big deal!

00:32:38.354 --> 00:32:42.188
I can't say I entirely
understand what I'm seeing here,

00:32:42.224 --> 00:32:43.953
but these people
don't seem to be suffering.

00:32:43.993 --> 00:32:45.790
Well, of course not.
They're happy people!

00:32:45.828 --> 00:32:47.420
Happy people!

00:32:47.463 --> 00:32:49.363
What's there to feel sad about?

00:32:49.398 --> 00:32:50.797
Look at them.

00:32:52.902 --> 00:32:54.563
They don't dare feel sad.

00:32:54.603 --> 00:32:57.003
If only they could,
that would be progress.

00:32:57.073 --> 00:32:59.007
Oh. The philosopher speaks.

00:32:59.075 --> 00:33:02.135
When I was
a respected philosopher,

00:33:02.178 --> 00:33:07.616
I celebrated the continuity,
the undeviation of Q life.

00:33:07.650 --> 00:33:10.710
I argued that our civilization
had achieved a purity

00:33:10.753 --> 00:33:13.517
that no other culture
had ever approached

00:33:13.556 --> 00:33:15.649
and it was wonderful...

00:33:15.691 --> 00:33:17.488
for a while.

00:33:17.526 --> 00:33:19.289
At the beginning of the new era,

00:33:19.328 --> 00:33:22.786
life as a Q was
a constant dialogue of discovery

00:33:22.832 --> 00:33:26.233
and issues and humor
from all over the universe,

00:33:26.268 --> 00:33:27.602
but look at them now.

00:33:27.735 --> 00:33:29.498
Listen to their dialogue now.

00:33:29.537 --> 00:33:31.334
I am afraid I cannot hear any.

00:33:31.372 --> 00:33:33.863
Because it has all been said.

00:33:33.908 --> 00:33:37.366
Everyone has heard everything,
seen everything.

00:33:37.411 --> 00:33:40.539
They haven't had to speak
to each other in ten millennia.

00:33:40.581 --> 00:33:43.209
There's nothing left to say.

00:33:43.250 --> 00:33:45.980
Well, I don't know about you,
but I appreciate a little peace

00:33:46.087 --> 00:33:47.679
and quiet now and again.

00:33:47.722 --> 00:33:50.122
It's ironic, isn't it, Q?

00:33:50.157 --> 00:33:51.647
I don't know what you mean.

00:33:51.692 --> 00:33:52.818
Of course you do.

00:33:52.860 --> 00:33:54.122
That you, of all people,

00:33:54.161 --> 00:33:56.220
should be arguing their case.

00:33:56.263 --> 00:33:59.664
I believe in the ultimate
purity of the Q.

00:33:59.700 --> 00:34:02.567
You, who were banned
from the Continuum

00:34:02.603 --> 00:34:05.265
and made mortal
to pay for your crimes?

00:34:05.306 --> 00:34:06.705
My penance has ended.

00:34:06.741 --> 00:34:08.174
I'm a born-again Q.

00:34:08.209 --> 00:34:11.269
That life is behind me.

00:34:11.312 --> 00:34:12.836
What a shame...

00:34:12.880 --> 00:34:15.815
because, in many ways,
that life inspired me.

00:34:15.850 --> 00:34:17.784
It did? I did?

00:34:17.818 --> 00:34:20.286
Oh, yes. You never knew that,
did you?

00:34:20.321 --> 00:34:22.346
You see, Captain,

00:34:22.390 --> 00:34:24.950
Q rebelled
against this existence

00:34:25.026 --> 00:34:27.256
by refusing to behave himself.

00:34:27.294 --> 00:34:28.784
He was out of control.

00:34:28.829 --> 00:34:32.321
He used his powers irresponsibly
and all for his own amusement,

00:34:32.366 --> 00:34:34.357
and he desperately
needed amusement

00:34:34.402 --> 00:34:37.064
because he could find
none here at home.

00:34:37.104 --> 00:34:39.470
And I paid the price
for my inappropriate behavior.

00:34:39.507 --> 00:34:43.238
No, no, we paid the price
by forcing you to stop,

00:34:43.277 --> 00:34:46.576
but for a moment there,
you really had our attention...

00:34:46.614 --> 00:34:48.548
my attention.

00:34:48.582 --> 00:34:51.312
You gave us something
to talk about,

00:34:51.352 --> 00:34:55.288
but then you surrendered
to the will of the Continuum

00:34:55.322 --> 00:34:57.847
like a good little Q,
and may I say you've become

00:34:57.892 --> 00:35:00.486
a fine, upstanding member
of the Continuum

00:35:00.528 --> 00:35:04.589
but I miss
the irrepressible Q...

00:35:04.632 --> 00:35:08.033
the one who forced me
to think.

00:35:14.008 --> 00:35:15.373
May I borrow this?

00:35:17.411 --> 00:35:20.209
This was the beginning
of my fall from grace.

00:35:20.247 --> 00:35:22.715
This was the last edition,
by the way.

00:35:22.750 --> 00:35:26.208
They shut down the presses
after I wrote that,

00:35:26.253 --> 00:35:27.880
but they couldn't
keep me silent.

00:35:27.922 --> 00:35:30.891
I continued to speak out
in favor of self-termination.

00:35:30.925 --> 00:35:32.392
That's when he lost his mind

00:35:32.426 --> 00:35:34.621
and started trying
to destroy himself.

00:35:34.662 --> 00:35:36.152
We had no choice
but to confine him

00:35:36.197 --> 00:35:37.960
but for his own safety.

00:35:38.032 --> 00:35:40.762
Not for my safety, for theirs.

00:35:40.801 --> 00:35:43.235
I was the greatest threat
the Continuum had ever known.

00:35:43.270 --> 00:35:45.704
They feared me so much,

00:35:45.740 --> 00:35:48.800
they had to lock me away
for eternity,

00:35:48.843 --> 00:35:51.539
and when they did that,
they were saying

00:35:51.579 --> 00:35:54.377
that the individual's rights
will be protected

00:35:54.415 --> 00:35:58.875
only so long as they don't
conflict with the state.

00:35:58.919 --> 00:36:03.447
Nothing is so dangerous
to a society.

00:36:03.491 --> 00:36:08.360
My life's work is complete,
but they force

00:36:08.395 --> 00:36:10.192
immortality on me,

00:36:10.231 --> 00:36:12.426
and when they do that,

00:36:12.466 --> 00:36:15.162
they cheapen
and denigrate my life

00:36:15.202 --> 00:36:19.036
and all life in the Continuum,
all life.

00:36:19.073 --> 00:36:22.406
Captain, you're an explorer.

00:36:22.443 --> 00:36:25.571
What if you had nothing left
to explore?

00:36:25.613 --> 00:36:29.379
Would you want to live forever
under those circumstances?

00:36:29.416 --> 00:36:30.815
You want me to prove to you

00:36:30.851 --> 00:36:33.046
that I suffer in terms
that you can equate

00:36:33.087 --> 00:36:35.146
with pain or disease.

00:36:35.189 --> 00:36:37.657
Look at us.

00:36:37.691 --> 00:36:42.788
When life has become futile,
meaningless, unendurable,

00:36:42.830 --> 00:36:45.958
it must be allowed to end.

00:36:46.000 --> 00:36:47.831
Can't you see, Captain?

00:36:47.868 --> 00:36:53.033
For us,
the disease is immortality.

00:36:59.680 --> 00:37:01.477
We rest our case, Captain.

00:37:03.184 --> 00:37:05.084
Very well.

00:37:05.119 --> 00:37:07.485
I'll make my ruling
in the morning.

00:37:07.521 --> 00:37:10.957
We'll be in recess until then.

00:37:45.059 --> 00:37:46.083
Trouble sleeping?

00:37:48.829 --> 00:37:51.957
Did you ever try warm
Kylerian goat's milk?

00:37:52.066 --> 00:37:54.967
Get out!

00:37:55.002 --> 00:37:56.833
Did you think about our offer?

00:37:56.871 --> 00:37:58.736
You mean your bribe.

00:37:58.772 --> 00:38:01.832
Merely an incentive to make
the proper decision.

00:38:01.876 --> 00:38:04.845
It'll play no part
in my deliberations.

00:38:04.879 --> 00:38:08.076
No.
I told them it wouldn't.

00:38:08.115 --> 00:38:10.845
That's why I talked them into
giving you what you asked for.

00:38:10.885 --> 00:38:12.011
You have my word.

00:38:12.052 --> 00:38:14.043
He won't go back to the cell.

00:38:14.088 --> 00:38:16.716
We'll assign someone
to look after him,

00:38:16.757 --> 00:38:18.520
whatever it takes.

00:38:18.559 --> 00:38:20.789
It's what you wanted, isn't it?

00:38:20.828 --> 00:38:23.922
That's what I wanted.

00:38:23.964 --> 00:38:26.660
So, you've won.

00:38:26.700 --> 00:38:28.827
Let's celebrate.

00:38:28.869 --> 00:38:30.166
Just you and me...

00:38:30.204 --> 00:38:31.762
the two of us.

00:38:31.805 --> 00:38:33.534
What?

00:38:33.574 --> 00:38:35.166
I'll take you home.

00:38:35.209 --> 00:38:36.176
Before you know it,

00:38:36.210 --> 00:38:37.939
you'll be scampering
across the meadow

00:38:38.012 --> 00:38:39.206
with your little puppies,

00:38:39.246 --> 00:38:41.544
the grass
beneath your bare feet.

00:38:41.582 --> 00:38:43.311
A man coming over the hill,

00:38:43.350 --> 00:38:45.511
way in the distance,
waves to you.

00:38:45.552 --> 00:38:47.611
You run to be in his arms,
and as you get closer,

00:38:47.655 --> 00:38:50.852
you see that it's... me.

00:38:50.891 --> 00:38:52.290
You?!

00:38:52.326 --> 00:38:54.886
Forget Mark.

00:38:54.929 --> 00:38:57.454
I know how to show a girl
a good time.

00:38:57.498 --> 00:38:59.363
How would you like
a ticker tape parade

00:38:59.400 --> 00:39:00.662
down Sri Lanka Boulevard?

00:39:00.701 --> 00:39:03.568
The Captain
who brought Voyager back...

00:39:03.604 --> 00:39:05.401
a celebrated hero.

00:39:05.439 --> 00:39:07.464
I never did anything like that
for Jean-Luc,

00:39:07.508 --> 00:39:10.568
but I feel very close to you.

00:39:10.611 --> 00:39:13.273
I'm not sure why.

00:39:13.314 --> 00:39:15.373
Maybe it's because
you have such authority

00:39:15.416 --> 00:39:18.977
and yet manage to preserve
your femininity so well.

00:39:25.459 --> 00:39:27.086
Leave.

00:39:29.129 --> 00:39:32.462
We'll talk about this
after the hearing tomorrow.

00:39:41.842 --> 00:39:43.673
I've tried to find
some way to reconcile

00:39:43.711 --> 00:39:47.306
all the conflicting emotions
I've felt during this hearing.

00:39:47.348 --> 00:39:50.840
My own aversion to suicide.

00:39:50.884 --> 00:39:54.285
My compassion
for your situation, Q.

00:39:54.321 --> 00:39:57.518
It hasn't been easy.

00:39:57.558 --> 00:40:01.050
I've tried to tell myself
that this is not about suicide,

00:40:01.095 --> 00:40:03.757
but about granting asylum,

00:40:03.797 --> 00:40:05.560
that I am not
personally being asked

00:40:05.599 --> 00:40:07.157
to perform euthanasia,

00:40:07.201 --> 00:40:09.362
and as technically true
as that may be,

00:40:09.403 --> 00:40:15.273
I cannot escape the moral
implications of my choices.

00:40:15.309 --> 00:40:17.971
I've also had to consider
that a decision to grant asylum,

00:40:18.045 --> 00:40:21.276
and the subsequent suicide
of a Q,

00:40:21.315 --> 00:40:24.250
might have a significant impact
on the Continuum.

00:40:24.284 --> 00:40:26.309
That such a decision

00:40:26.353 --> 00:40:29.550
could change
the nature of an entire society,

00:40:29.590 --> 00:40:32.616
whether it be a favorable
or unfavorable change,

00:40:32.659 --> 00:40:34.854
disturbs me greatly.

00:40:37.965 --> 00:40:41.958
But then there are the rights of
the individual in this matter.

00:40:42.002 --> 00:40:44.698
I don't believe that you are
mentally unbalanced,

00:40:44.738 --> 00:40:49.869
and I do believe that you
are suffering intolerably.

00:40:51.979 --> 00:40:54.004
Under these conditions,

00:40:54.048 --> 00:40:57.449
I find it impossible
to support immortality forced

00:40:57.484 --> 00:40:58.883
on an individual by the state.

00:40:58.919 --> 00:41:00.011
The unforeseen disruption

00:41:00.120 --> 00:41:05.456
that may occur in the Continuum
is not enough, in my opinion,

00:41:05.492 --> 00:41:09.986
to justify any additional
suffering by this individual.

00:41:11.999 --> 00:41:15.332
So... I hereby grant you asylum.

00:41:17.504 --> 00:41:19.904
May I see you in your chambers,
Captain?

00:41:19.940 --> 00:41:22.101
You've been in my chambers
enough for one visit, sir.

00:41:22.142 --> 00:41:23.302
A sidebar, Your Honor.

00:41:23.343 --> 00:41:24.742
Only for a moment.

00:41:24.778 --> 00:41:26.336
She ruled in my favor.

00:41:26.380 --> 00:41:27.779
You made a promise.

00:41:36.623 --> 00:41:39.717
Nothing happened... nothing!

00:41:39.760 --> 00:41:42.627
My powers are gone!

00:41:42.663 --> 00:41:45.188
I'm mortal.

00:41:50.104 --> 00:41:52.595
Well, so much
for ticker tape parades.

00:41:52.639 --> 00:41:54.106
I'm not finished.

00:41:54.141 --> 00:41:56.006
Q...

00:41:56.043 --> 00:41:58.773
now that you're mortal,

00:41:58.812 --> 00:42:01.372
you have a new existence
to explore,

00:42:01.415 --> 00:42:03.849
an entirely new state of being

00:42:03.884 --> 00:42:06.785
filled with the mysteries
of mortal life,

00:42:06.820 --> 00:42:08.947
pleasures
you've never felt before.

00:42:09.056 --> 00:42:12.822
I like this life, Q.

00:42:12.860 --> 00:42:15.761
You might, too.

00:42:15.796 --> 00:42:19.357
Think hard
before you give it up.

00:42:25.205 --> 00:42:27.696
This hearing is adjourned.

00:42:28.976 --> 00:42:32.776
Captain's Log,
Stardate 49301.2.

00:42:32.813 --> 00:42:35.543
We have assigned quarters
to our new passenger,

00:42:35.582 --> 00:42:38.983
who has entered his name on
our crew manifest as "Quinn."

00:42:39.052 --> 00:42:41.520
I'm anxious to engage him
in ship activities

00:42:41.555 --> 00:42:44.080
as soon as possible.

00:42:44.124 --> 00:42:45.591
How about Stellar Cartography?

00:42:45.626 --> 00:42:47.526
We could shut down
Stellar Cartography

00:42:47.561 --> 00:42:49.392
with all the knowledge
he'd bring to the job.

00:42:49.429 --> 00:42:50.828
Well, that's going
to be a problem

00:42:50.864 --> 00:42:52.798
with just about everything
we assign him to.

00:42:52.833 --> 00:42:55.768
There's got to be something on
board that...

00:42:55.802 --> 00:42:56.996
Sick Bay to Captain Janeway.

00:42:57.104 --> 00:42:58.093
Go ahead.

00:42:58.138 --> 00:43:00.003
Captain, I think you should
come down to Sick Bay.

00:43:00.040 --> 00:43:03.476
Mr. Quinn is here.
I'm afraid he's dying.

00:43:09.550 --> 00:43:11.313
There's nothing you can do?

00:43:11.351 --> 00:43:14.286
He's ingested a rare form
of Nogatch hemlock.

00:43:14.321 --> 00:43:15.982
There is no known cure.

00:43:17.591 --> 00:43:20.856
I'm sorry to disappoint you,
Captain,

00:43:20.894 --> 00:43:23.089
but I would only
have been pretending

00:43:23.130 --> 00:43:26.896
to fit in
to this mortal existence.

00:43:26.934 --> 00:43:30.370
This is my final gift
to my people.

00:43:30.404 --> 00:43:36.968
Oh, tell them those were
my last words.

00:43:37.010 --> 00:43:41.674
I dearly thank you
for making this poss...

00:43:51.625 --> 00:43:52.990
Doctor,

00:43:53.060 --> 00:43:55.460
do you generally keep samples
of fatal poisons in storage?

00:43:55.495 --> 00:43:57.292
No.

00:43:57.331 --> 00:43:59.993
The replicators
will not produce them either.

00:44:00.033 --> 00:44:04.663
So how did he get his hands
on Nogatch hemlock?

00:44:06.206 --> 00:44:07.764
I got it for him.

00:44:09.309 --> 00:44:12.540
You assisted his suicide?

00:44:12.579 --> 00:44:13.546
Illogical, Tuvok?

00:44:13.580 --> 00:44:15.377
I don't think so.

00:44:15.415 --> 00:44:16.939
By demanding to end his life,

00:44:17.017 --> 00:44:19.417
he taught me a little something
about my own.

00:44:19.453 --> 00:44:21.114
He was right when he said

00:44:21.154 --> 00:44:23.554
the Continuum scared me
back in line.

00:44:23.590 --> 00:44:26.616
I didn't have his courage
or his convictions.

00:44:26.660 --> 00:44:30.289
He called me "irrepressible."

00:44:30.330 --> 00:44:34.130
This was a man
who was truly irrepressible.

00:44:34.167 --> 00:44:37.034
I only hope
I make a worthy student.

00:44:38.805 --> 00:44:40.966
I imagine the Continuum
won't be very happy

00:44:41.041 --> 00:44:42.633
with you, Q.

00:44:42.676 --> 00:44:45.702
I certainly hope not.

00:44:45.746 --> 00:44:48.579
Au revoir, Madam Captain.

00:44:48.615 --> 00:44:50.640
We will meet again.
